mk("Orin_Pensinata.md", "Orin Pensinata", "2", "Book 7", "Book 12", "Books 7-12 (chapter files)",
   "Amos_Pensinata.md, Korinne_Pescos.md, Zara_Rimaros.md, Kasper_Irios.md",
   "A calm silver-rank guild adventurer, Amos Pensinata's nephew, who rises to gold and survives Team Storm Shredder's losses.",
   ["A silver-ranker \"most notable for his famous uncle, Amos\", who nods to one of the princesses in the surge expedition (Book 7, Ch47 L39).",
    "Quiet, stable and respected in the guild team: he restrains an angry companion with \"Complications. Best left alone\" (Book 7, Ch47 L51-53, L72); he is the steadfast one, fresh from a rank-up (Book 7, Ch48 L7).",
    "His first meeting with Jason came through Vesper Rimaros's arranged meeting with Kasper Irios (Book 9, Ch25 L79).",
    "Orin and Kalif's team is led by Korinne Pescos; they first met Jason in a mixed-force expedition (Book 9, Ch24 L49). The team is Storm Shredder, built around buffed high-damage ranged specialists (Book 9, Ch84 L9; Book 10, Ch64 L9).",
    "He goes on Jason's journey because his uncle insisted, and he is slow-spoken (\"My uncle is a hard man, but he likes soft beds\", Book 9, Ch24 L35; Book 9, Ch28 L87-112).",
    "In Book 11 Storm Shredder loses two members; Orin is the only one strong enough to force Zara back from the fighting (Book 11, Ch32 L73-74). After the zone, Amos takes Orin and the scout Rosa back to Rimaros (Book 11, Ch68 L378).",
    "By Book 12 Orin has reached gold rank and is in a team with Kasper Irios and friends (Book 12, Ch12 L61); Hils Jaramaris's friend Orin who went on to travel with Asano is presumably him (Book 12, Ch49 L5)."],
   "Stoic and slow to speak; he keeps a team steady and says only what needs saying.")

mk("Baseph_and_the_Rimaros_Children.md", "Baseph, Dara, Zareen and Joseph", "2", "Book 7", "Book 9", "Books 7-9 (chapter files)",
   "Liara_Rimaros.md, Zara_Rimaros.md, Soramir.md, ../06_Places/Rimaros.md",
   "Liara Rimaros's husband and their three silver-rank children.",
   ["Baseph is Liara's husband, silver rank, met leaving her townhouse (Book 7, Ch17 L20). In Book 8 he hammers a pipe to draw raiders (Book 8, Ch33 L64), fears what lies below because it is people who died because of what he did (Book 8, Ch37 L77) and is saved by Jason (Book 8, Ch62 L51). He holds Liara's hand under the table (Book 8, Ch63 L3).",
    "Dara is the eldest, a one-star adventurer happy to hunt monsters, with Liara's height and Baseph's dark copper hair and eyes, a muscular frontline combatant (Book 8, Ch62 L39).",
    "Zareen is the middle child, physically smaller, with the royal family's sapphire hair and eyes, a politics enthusiast close to Vesper and a three-star adventurer (Book 8, Ch62 L36).",
    "Joseph is the youngest and only son, an administrative official with the Amouz family business interests like his father (Book 8, Ch62 L32); he wants to meet the man who saved his father (Book 8, Ch62 L51).",
    "Dara's later remark about \"the one from up north\" with the elf twins refers to Rick (Book 9, Ch11 L60)."],
   "A warm family dinner: Zareen sharp and strategic, Dara blunt and cheerful, Joseph mild.")

grp("Minor_Cast_Order_of_Redeeming_Light.md", "Order of Redeeming Light Members", "2", "Book 7", "Book 11", "Books 7, 8, 11 (chapter files)",
    "../Melody_Jain.md, ../../05_Organisations/Cults_and_Orders.md",
    "The named members of Melody Jain's Sea of Storms contingent. Compare Melody's own file for the order's history.",
    [("Sendira", ["Melody's second in command and the person she trusts most, not the most imaginative subordinate (Book 7, Ch58 L38; Book 8, Ch9 L17; Book 8, Ch33 L15). She defends Melody against rivals (Book 8, Ch9 L50) and activates the aura beacon in the grab (Book 8, Ch13 L51; Book 8, Ch16 L86)."]),
     ("Laront", ["The order's church advisor, a young-looking human priest of Purity who never passed through the flames, so he can visit cities safely (Book 7, Ch58 L38; Book 8, Ch3 L38). He buys information from an Adventure Society functionary (Book 8, Ch3 L39-58) and says \"I am the church's eyes\" (Book 8, Ch18 L14)."]),
     ("Esteban Galo", ["A gold-rank adventurer who has seen more of the order's operation than Melody and Laront like (Book 8, Ch17 L5, L29)."]),
     ("Fila", ["A cell leader who says Melody advances her personal agenda and risks the order's assets (Book 8, Ch9 L30); she warns that most of their forces will be lost (Book 8, Ch9 L49)."]),
     ("Ramona", ["A human who was once a celestine, her hair and eyes now sunshine blonde and blue (Book 8, Ch9 L11); she clears tunnels with stone powers and blames Sendira for the beacon (Book 8, Ch13 L47-51; Book 8, Ch14 L71). She later projects a dome in Miriam's team, Moon's Edge (Book 11, Ch46 L11)."]),
     ("Rhett and Jaime", ["Silver-rank members who frogmarch a prisoner and are talkative and more human than the compelled majority (Book 8, Ch16 L28; Book 8, Ch29 L26-29). Jaime thinks torture is wrong because they \"worship Purity, not Pain\" (Book 8, Ch33 L45)."]),
     ("Caitlyn, Heston, Marika and Elise", ["Caitlyn, Heston, Marika and Elise challenge Melody's leadership (Book 8, Ch18 L4-34). Caitlyn's group thinks pain purifies the soul (Book 8, Ch33 L45). Elise and Marika are cell leaders who each try to seize control of the order after the island operation fails (Book 8, Ch44 L29-40)."]),
     ("Kelleigh", ["A blank-faced, dedicated member of Melody's cell who delivers a prisoner (Book 8, Ch18 L68) and quotes resonating-force siege weapons (Book 8, Ch33 L24, L47)."])])

